    "updated_at": "2023-01-18T20:54:20Z",
    "body": "> > solve https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/3163 and https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/2407\r\n> \r\n> I understand that this option will solve the https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/2407, but I do not know how is https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/3163 related to this request ...\r\n\r\nAh, that was a typo, fixed now.\r\n\r\nThe way I see it there is a feature request here for a module variable to either count or not count the initial shell in the SHLVL. This is probably a personal developer preference and so should be exposed as an option. However, there is a complicating problem that different shells have already chosen whether or not to count the outermost shell in `$SHLVL`, and different shells have chosen differently. This means that even for users that don't explicitly set a variable like `adjust` they get different values in different environments. So ISTM that to keep it simple with one module variable, Starship would first have to normalize depending on the running shell.",
